From e463a50a793fcee214de203ec40cb6390664432e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jayneelatintel <jayneel.vora@intel.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 19:34:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] dist-tp: accumulate the ring all-reduce on the host

Accumulate peer contributions into a host buffer and write the reduced
result back to the boundary tensor once, instead of uploading each
contribution to a scratch tensor and submitting a GPU ADD per ring step.
On backends with a high submit latency (Vulkan on an integrated GPU)
those submissions dominated decode. Also drops the per-backend
synchronize before dist_allreduce_fallback, which its async get and
merged synchronize now cover.

The collective boundary predicate keeps every boundary node. Filtering
the boundary set again by tensor name skips required all-reduces and
gives wrong output.
